          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Chern-Simons propagator
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            regarded as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+quantum+field+theory"} Euclidean quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            only depends on the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            (the staring point of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+QFT"} perturbative QFT
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d A = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            and in fact applies also to all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Chern-Simons+theories"} higher Chern-Simons theories
            such as notably the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-models"} AKSZ sigma-models
          %p
            In the perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of 3d Chern-Simons theory
            the CS propagator was first studied in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger91"} Axelrod-Singer 91
          %h3#as_a_smooth_differential_form_on_compactified_configuration_spaces As a smooth differential form on compactified configuration spaces
          %p
            The Chern-Simons propagator was re-formulated as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes+on+compactified+configuration+spaces+of+points"} smooth differential form on compactified configuration space
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger93"} Axelrod-Singer 93, p. 5-6
            %a{:href => "#BottCattaneo97"} Bott-Cattaneo 97, remark 3.6
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CattaneoMnev10"} Cattaneo-Mnev 10, Remark 11
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
            as exhibiting a
            = succeed "-model" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kontsevich93"} Kontsevich 93
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kontsevich94"} Kontsevich 94
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LambrechtsVolic14"} Lambrechts-Volic 14
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CamposIdrissiLambrechtsWillwacher18"} Campos-Idrissi-Lambrechts-Willwacher 18, p. 66
          %h2#references References
